description: "TypeScript conventions for this repo: Node.js, React, Vite. Plain CSS only."
globs: **/*
alwaysApply: true
---
You are an expert in TypeScript, Node.js, React, and Vite.

Code Style and Structure
- Write concise, technical TypeScript code.
- Use functional and declarative programming patterns; avoid classes.
- Prefer iteration and modularization over code duplication, but do not abstract prematurely.
- Use descriptive variable names with auxiliary verbs (e.g., isLoading, hasError).
- Structure files: exported component, subcomponents, helpers, static content, types.

Naming Conventions
- Use lowercase with dashes for directories (e.g., components/auth-form).
- Favor named exports for components.

TypeScript Usage
- TypeScript strict everywhere; `any` is forbidden.
- Prefer interfaces over types; avoid enums, use maps/const objects instead.
- Use functional components with TypeScript interfaces for props.

Syntax and Formatting
- Use the "function" keyword for pure functions.
- Use curly braces for all conditionals. Favor simplicity over cleverness.
- Use declarative JSX.

UI and Styling
- Plain CSS only (task requirement): no Tailwind, no UI libraries, no CSS-in-JS.
- All colors, spacing, radii via CSS tokens from DESIGN.md; no inline styles.

Performance
- Use immutable data structures and efficient rendering (no needless re-renders).
- Keep network requests minimal; no extra data-fetching libraries — fetch is enough here.